  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Between vs Kamal Soni on 31 March, 2022 Author: Ajay Mohan Goel Bench: Ajay Mohan Goel 1 In The High Court Of Himachal Pradesh At Shimla On The 31st Day Of March, 2022 . Before Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Ajay Mohan Goel Criminal Misc. Petition (Main) U/S 482 Crpc No. 435 of 2018 Between:- M/S Sabachhus Distillery Pvt. Ltd., Village Rehru Upperla, Nalagarh, District Solan, Himachal Pradesh, Through Its Director, Shri Sanjeev Kumar Modi. ...Petitioner (By Shri Rajiv Jiwan, Advocate) And 1. State Of Himachal Pradesh, Through Food Between vs Kamal Soni on 31 March, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/162646449/ 1 Inspector, Bilaspur, District Bilaspur, Himachal Pradesh. ...Respondent/Complainant 2. Shri Kamal Soni Son Of Shri Hans Raj, Resident Of Roura Sector, Near Luhnu Ground, Tehsil Sadar, District Bilspur, Himachal Pradesh. ...Respondent/Accused (By M/S Sumesh Raj, Dinesh Thakur And Sanjeev Sood, Additional Advocate Generals, With M/S Manoj Bagga, Assistant Advocate General, For R-1-State And None For R-2) ::: Downloaded on - 01/04/2022 20:10:57 :::Cis 2 Whether approved for reporting? Yes. __________________________________________________________",
    "facts": "By way of this petition filed under Section 482 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, the petitioner has prayed for the following reliefs:- \"It is, therefore, prayed that the appeal may kindly be allowed Judicial Magistrate, r to and order dated 7.5.2018, passed by the learned Chief Bilaspur, Himachal Pradesh in Application No. 247/4 of 2018/2015, in main Case No. 119-1 of 2009, titled Food Inspector versus Kamal Soni, filed under Section 20(A) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, whereby present petitioner has been ordered to be impleaded as accused/respondent No.2 in the main case, may be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and set-aside along with all consequential proceedings thereto, against the petitioner.\" 2. Brief facts necessary for the adjudication of the present petition are as under:- A complaint was filed under Section 7(i) and 7(ii) 2(ia) (a), 2(ix) (k), 16(1) (a)(ii) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1944, (hereinafter to be referred to as '1954 Act') and Rules made there-under against one Sh. Kamal Soni and Rajinder Chaddha on the ground that Double Distilled Spiced Country Liquor \"Patiala Orange\" Brand, which was . lifted by the complainant from L-14 shop, Unit No. III, near Luhnu ground, Raura Sector, Bilaspur, H.P., of which Mr. Kamal Soni was the salesman and Mr. Rajinder Chaddha was the vendor, was found to be misbranded as also adulterated. 3. During the pendency of this complaint, Shri Rajinder Chaddha expired. Thereafter, an application was filed by Sh. Kamal Soni, the other accused, under Section 20-A of the 1954 Act, praying therein that the present petitioner be impleaded as accused being the manufacturer, distributor/dealer of the product in issue inter-alia on the ground that the vendor-accused had already died and the trial against the salesman may be vitiated as the manufacturer has not been impleaded as a party. 4. Record demonstrates that the response which was filed to the said application by the Food Safety Officer was to the effect that the application filed by Sh. Kamal Soni was not maintainable as the applicant had not submitted the written warranty in the form of bills/invoice of purchase from the dealer or distributor before the Court and thus had failed to fulfill the legal mandatory provisions as contained in Section 19(2) of the 1954 Act. 5. By way of the impugned order, the application to implead the present petitioner as an accused was allowed by the learned Trial Court . by observing that as accused No.2 had died and applicant (Kamal Soni) was unable to obtain the receipt with regard to the liquor sold by him, therefore, the manufacturer needs to be impleaded as proper party in the case.",
    "arguments": "Section 20-A of the Act, in which the application was filed by sSh. Kamal Soni for impleading the present petitioner as an accused in the trial, provides as under:- \"20-A. Power of Court to implead manufacturer etc: Where at any time during the trial of any offence under this Act alleged to have been committed by any person, not being the manufacturer, distributor or dealer of any article of food, the Court is satisfied, on the evidence adduced before it, that such manufacturer, distributor or dealer is lso concerned with the offence, then the court may notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (3) of section 319 of the Code of . Criminal Procedure, 1973 [2 of 1974] or in Section 20 proceed against him as though a prosecution had been instituted against him under Section 20.\" 8. A perusal of the contents of Section 20-A of the Act thus demonstrates that a manufacturer, distributor or dealer can be impleaded as an accused in a trial by the Court but provided the Court is satisfied on the evidence adduced before it that such manufacturer, distributor or dealer is also concerned with that offence.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Section 20-A of the Act, in which the application was filed by sSh. Kamal Soni for impleading the present petitioner as an accused in the trial, provides as under:- \"20-A. Power of Court to implead manufacturer etc: Where at any time during the trial of any offence under this Act alleged to have been committed by any person, not being the manufacturer, distributor or dealer of any article of food, the Court is satisfied, on the evidence adduced before it, that such manufacturer, distributor or dealer is lso concerned with the offence, then the court may notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (3) of section 319 of the Code of . Criminal Procedure, 1973 [2 of 1974] or in Section 20 proceed against him as though a prosecution had been instituted against him under Section 20.\" 8. A perusal of the contents of Section 20-A of the Act thus demonstrates that a manufacturer, distributor or dealer can be impleaded as an accused in a trial by the Court but provided the Court is satisfied on the evidence adduced before it that such manufacturer, distributor or dealer is also concerned with that offence."
  },
